112 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 74 0 R
/E (This project implements 2D spatial convolution using a standard 3x3 Laplacian sharpening kernel on raw 8-bit grayscale images. Each output pixel is computed as a weighted sum of its 3x3 neighborhood in the input image, using the following kernel:)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
113 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 74 0 R
/E (The center weight of 5 amplifies the original pixel intensity, while the four negative weights subtract contributions from its direct \(top, bottom, left, right\) neighbors. This effectively enhances high-frequency spatial components \(edges and fine details\) while preserving the overall brightness. Boundary pixels use zero-padding \(pixels outside the image boundary are treated as 0\).)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
114 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 74 0 R
/E (The primary objective is to implement, parallelize, optimize, and benchmark this convolution operation across four paradigms: Sequential \(CPU\), OpenMP \(CPU, multi-threaded\), Optimized OpenMP \(CPU, SIMD + branch elimination\), and CUDA \(GPU\), and to determine whether parallel execution actually improves performance.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
