412 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (Key Observation: The PCIe data transfer overhead dominates the total CUDA execution time, accounting for 81-92% of the total time. The GPU kernel itself runs 5-13x faster than even the total GPU time. This is a classic characteristic of memory-bound, low- compute-intensity operations -- the convolution kernel is computationally simple \(5 multiplications and 5 additions per pixel\), so the GPU finishes the computation extremely quickly but must wait for data to arrive from and return to host memory.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [21]
>>
endobj
413 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (The kernel-to-total speedup ratio worsens as image size grows \(from 5.4x for Small to 13.0x for Large\) because the data transfer volume scales linearly with pixel count while the kernel benefits from GPU-level parallelism that absorbs the additional workload efficiently.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
