441 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 84 0 R
/E (In the naive implementation, every pixel \(including interior pixels\) executes 4 conditional boundary checks per kernel coefficient \(if nr >= 0 and nr < height and nc >= 0 and nc < width\). For a 7680x4320 image, this means approximately 298 million branch evaluations, of which over 99.9% are trivially true \(interior pixels are never near the boundary\).)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [22]
>>
