/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 85 0 R
/T (For the Small dataset \(1920x1080 = approximately 2M pixels\), the basic OpenMP speedup is only 1.67x on 2 threads \(83.5% efficiency\). This is partly because thread creation, scheduling, and synchronization overhead constitute a non-negligible fraction of the approximately 40ms execution time. For extremely small images, this overhead could exceed the computation time, making parallelization counterproductive.)
/E (For the Small dataset \(1920x1080 = approximately 2M pixels\), the basic OpenMP speedup is only 1.67x on 2 threads \(83.5% efficiency\). This is partly because thread creation, scheduling, and synchronization overhead constitute a non-negligible fraction of the approximately 40ms execution time. For extremely small images, this overhead could exceed the computation time, making parallelization counterproductive.)
